    none stored. No hit points printed; none stored.
  - xp_table from the "Voodoo Priest, Jungle Elf & Totem Warrior" ladder,
    printed 168 (cache p169), lower bounds; identical to voodoo-priest''s
    stored table. In a pairing the O.C.C.''s ladder wins where it states one.
  - Attributes: I.Q. 3D6+2, M.E. 3D6, M.A. 4D6, P.S. 2D6+3, P.P. 3D6+3,
    P.E. 3D6, P.B. 4D6, Spd 4D6, as printed.
  - P.P.E.: P.E. number plus 1D4x10, +1D6 per level. I.S.P.: M.E. plus
    1D4x10, +2D4 per level. Major psionic, six powers from Sensitive,
    Physical or Healer (catalog category Healing). The book states no
    further powers with level, so no powers_schedule.
  - Biomancy (ability 3): no spells at level 1; one at level 2 from spell
    level 1, then one each level from levels up to experience level minus
    one. Stored as spells_starting 0 and a spells_schedule of 14 entries
    (levels 2-15), each drawing from the named BIOMANCY list (all 24
    Biomancy catalog spells) with an explicit spell_levels cap of 1 to
    L-1. The named list keeps general invocations out, since the book says
    Biomancy spells only.
  - spell_traditions_allowed ["biomancy"] is stated although this class''s
    own picks are list-bound: it unions into a paired spell O.C.C., whose
    spells_schedule replaces the race''s, so a jungle elf Ley Line Walker or
    Mystic can still reach Biomancy spells through its level-gated picks.
    That is an approximation of the book''s additive racial grant, which is
    lost in such a pairing; the race-alone ladder is exact.
  - The note that Warlock, Mind Melter and Shifter/Summoner elves have no
    Biomancy is a restriction line, not enforced: paired with the Mind
    Melter (no magic block) the race''s Biomancy ladder still applies.
  - Bonuses: +1 to resist magic stored on spell_magic and ritual_magic; +1
    vs psionics; +2 vs horror factor.
  - Skills of Note: Wilderness Survival at 55% (catalog 30, so +25);
    Dragonese/Elven (+25%) -> Language: Dragonese at 75; Faerie (+20%) has
    no catalog row, so it is a one-pick Language: Other at 70 with a note.
    The 75% who are skilled at archery and targeting is not a grant to
    every elf; it is a natural ability line only.
  - O.C.C.s (ability 8): the book lists what is available with percentages
    summing to 100%, so it is stored as occ_restrictions.only with the ids
    in the catalog: biomancer, wilderness-scout, the ten Conversion Book
    warlocks (the book names Earth, Air and Water, and Fire at 0.5%),
    ley-line-walker, mind-melter, mystic, shifter (Shifter/Summoner),
    totem-warrior-south-american, tribal-shaman (the book''s "Jungle Shaman
    (new O.C.C.)"; Tribal Shaman is the only shaman O.C.C. in this book),
    stone-master. NOT in the catalog on the day of drafting, so not
    listed and currently refused: Herbalist or Druid (Rifts England; the
    catalog''s druid is the Palladium Fantasy one), Temporal Wizard (Rifts
    England), African Priest, Rain Maker and Medicine Man (Rifts Africa).
    Each needs adding here when it is imported. "Wilderness Scout or
    equivalent" is read as the Wilderness Scout only. The percentage table
    is in the Lore.
  - Equipment: this list takes priority over the O.C.C.''s. Stored:
    clothing, backpack, one bow (short or long), two simple biomancer
    weapons from the lesser bio-weapons (enchanted wooden club, sword or
    spear), one light armor (wood or chitin). Not stored: arrows (no count
    printed), the second archaic weapon (unnamed), the "one major biomancer
    weapon" alternative to the two simple ones, medium armor (no catalog
    row) and the organically grown pouch (no pouch row); these are in
    side_effects.
  - No starting money printed for the race; none stored.
