## Lore

Outsiders know little of the jungle elves, of biomancy or of Maga. Most take them for a strange cousin of the Palladium World''s elves and faerie folk, though no such race is known there. The elves'' own legends tell of a primeval world ruled by the Tree of Life, a tree the size of a mountain, and they call themselves the sons and daughters, or Champions, of the Tree. Some scholars think an advanced alien civilization made them, perhaps a rival of the makers of the Millennium Trees; wherever jungle elves thrive, Millennium Trees do not grow, and the reverse. The elves admire the trees of England from afar and call them cousins, as they call all plant life their brothers and cousins.

Jungle elves live as nomadic tribes or in permanent communities. Settled elves reshape their surroundings into living cities of interlocked trees and brush and breed new plants to serve the community; even elves who practise no biomancy can modify living things to suit their needs. Maga island is the largest and most powerful of their communities.

Many love to wander, especially through jungle and forest. Nomadic tribes roam the Amazon, and one or two elves, or a tiny band of no more than 3D6, may turn up anywhere in South America - occasionally as far north as the old Canadian Empire, usually by magic or sea to avoid vampire-infested Mexico, and as far east as Africa.

**Alignment:** Any.

**Typical O.C.C.s among jungle elves:** Biomancer 20%; Wilderness Scout or equivalent 15% (most high-tech skills replaced with Domestic, Wilderness, W.P. or Physical skills); Warlock 15% (Earth, Air and Water; only 0.5% are Fire Warlocks, often shunned); Ley Line Walker 10%; Herbalist or Druid (Rifts England) 10%; Mind Melter 10%; Mystic 5%; Shifter/Summoner 3%; Totem Warrior 3%; Jungle Shaman or African Priest (Rifts Africa) 3%; African Rain Maker or Medicine Man (Rifts Africa) 2%; Stone Master (Rifts Atlantis) 2%; Temporal Wizard (Rifts England) 2%. Reduce or eliminate most high-tech skills from whichever O.C.C. is chosen.

## GM Notes

The Warlock, Mind Melter and Shifter/Summoner are the typical jungle elf occupations with no Biomancy; the app does not strip the racial Biomancy ladder from those pairings, so remove it by hand if you follow the book. An elf who turns to technology and machines, or lives in a tech city, loses Biomancy until 1D4 years after returning to the jungle ways.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'jungle-elf');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'jungle-elf';

